      "ReviewText": "Out of the box, 15 minutes to assemble. I'll have to wait till the trim string is used up, to see how difficult it will be to respool it with new string. On initial start, had to pull a few more times than stated, but after that, 2 to 3 pulls to start. Trimmed around my entire house, driveway, walkways, and lawn edges without issue and no loss in power. Cutting width was wide and helped get the job done efficiently. I've had straight shaft trimmers, but I like this curved design much better. Handling was comfortable and evenly balanced. My next fill up, I'm going to try premium gas to mix with the oil to see if it'll run a bit smoother. Regular unleaded seemed a little rough, but not a deal breaker at all.",
      "Title": "More than suitable for home use",
      "UserNickname": "Mr  Sixofnine",
